# Commander keyboard - the microcontroller circuit, soldered straight onto the keyboard PCB in place of the Arduino
# Micro module (U1 of the Altium design).
#
# Since 2026-11-15 (cost target): STC8H8K64U-45I-LQFP32 (LCSC C5210757, about 0.35 USD in volume) instead of the
# ATmega32U4 (about 3.30 USD).  It runs from the same 5 V, so the 84 infra-red LEDs and phototransistors of the matrix
# see the same levels as on the prototype.  It needs no crystal (USB clock recovered from the bus), no reset circuit
# and no ISP pads: firmware goes in over the USB-C itself, through STC's USB boot loader, entered by holding the BOOT
# button (P3.2 to ground) while the cable is plugged in.  THE FIRMWARE IS NEW: the Arduino sketch of the prototype
# does not run on this 8051-core chip; the pin table below is what it has to read and drive (see the README).
#
# Kept: USB-C (device side, 5.1 k on both CC pins), the ESD array, the 22 ohm series resistors, the resettable fuse
# (750 mA: the 84 infra-red LEDs draw about 0.56 A when all are on), the decoupling.
# Net names are still the ARDUINO pin names (D0..D13, A0..A5, MISO / SCK / MOSI) the prototype used: they name the
# matrix lines, not chip pins any more.  References are in a 200-block (no collision with the Altium parts).
SHEET kbd_mcu

# --- microcontroller ---
# Chip sides on the board (U201 on the bottom face, turned so that): north pins 1-8, east 9-16, south 17-24, west 25-32
#   north (west -> east): A0..A5 rows on pins 1-6, MOSI on 7      (the row lines end to the north-west)
#   east  (north -> south): SCK, supply, USB, BOOT, MISO          (USB-C and the SPI line ends are to the east)
#   south (east -> west): SS_RXLED, D0 (infra-red enable), D2, D3, D4, D5
#   west  (south -> north): D6..D13                               (the column lines end to the west)
U201 STC8H_LQFP32:STC8H8K64U 10=VCC5 11=VCC5 12=GND
P U201 8=UCAP 13=USB_MCU_DM 14=USB_MCU_DP 15=BOOT_N
# matrix rows (6), driven as outputs
P U201 1=A0 2=A1 3=A2 4=A3 5=A4 6=A5
# matrix columns (16), read as inputs
P U201 7=MOSI 9=SCK 16=MISO 17=SS_RXLED 19=D2_SDA 20=D3_SCL 21=D4 22=D5
P U201 25=D6 26=D7 27=D8 28=D9 29=D10 30=D11 31=D12 32=D13
# infra-red LED enable (to Q1 through the jumper J1)
P U201 18=D0_RX
# spare
NC U201 23
# (pin 24: the power-key output, see 09_kbd_powerkey.net)

# --- supply: USB bus power only ---
F201 PTC:750mA VBUS_USB VCC5
# UCAP: the chip's USB regulator (0.1 - 10 uF to ground)
C201 1uF_0603 UCAP GND
C203 100nF_0603 VCC5 GND
C204 100nF_0603 VCC5 GND
C205 4.7uF_0603 VCC5 GND
# ADC reference pin tied to +5 V (no analogue input is used), with its own capacitor
C206 100nF_0603 VCC5 GND

# --- boot: hold while plugging in USB -> STC USB boot loader ("STC USB Writer (HID1)" in STC-ISP) ---
R206 10K_0603 VCC5 BOOT_N
SW201 TACT:BOOT 1=BOOT_N 2=GND

# --- USB-C, device side, on the left edge of the board: NOT FITTED since 2026-11-18 (the keyboard reaches the
#     mainboard over the harness J202, 09_kbd_powerkey.net); kept for flashing / testing from a PC, never with J202 ---
J201 USBC16:DNP A1=GND A12=GND B1=GND B12=GND SH=GND A4=VBUS_USB A9=VBUS_USB B4=VBUS_USB B9=VBUS_USB
P J201 A5=KB_CC1 B5=KB_CC2 A6=USB_CON_DP B6=USB_CON_DP A7=USB_CON_DM B7=USB_CON_DM
NC J201 A8 B8
R201 DNP KB_CC1 GND
R202 DNP KB_CC2 GND
U202 USBLC6-2SC6 1=USB_CON_DP 6=USB_CON_DP 3=USB_CON_DM 4=USB_CON_DM 2=GND 5=VBUS_USB
C210 4.7uF_0603 VBUS_USB GND
# series resistors at the MCU end of the two data lines
R203 22R_0603 USB_CON_DP USB_MCU_DP
R204 22R_0603 USB_CON_DM USB_MCU_DM
